# ==============================================================================
# DEPLOYMENT ENVIRONMENT NOTES
# ==============================================================================
#
# LOCAL DEVELOPMENT (.env.local):
#  - Copy this file to .env.local
#  - Fill in local/development Firebase project credentials
#  - Use development API keys with generous rate limits
#  - Set NODE_ENV=development
#  - NEXT_PUBLIC_BASE_URL=http://localhost:3000
#
# STAGING DEPLOYMENT:
#  - Create separate Firebase project for staging
#  - Use staging API keys
#  - Set NODE_ENV=staging
#  - NEXT_PUBLIC_BASE_URL=https://staging.lecture-helper.com
#  - Enable Sentry for error tracking
#  - Reduce API quotas to catch issues before production
#
# PRODUCTION DEPLOYMENT:
#  - Use production Firebase project with strict security rules
#  - Rotate secrets regularly (monthly recommended)
#  - Set NODE_ENV=production
#  - NEXT_PUBLIC_BASE_URL=https://lecture-helper.com
#  - Enable Sentry with appropriate sampling rates
#  - Monitor costs closely (Gemini, FAL.ai have per-request costs)
#  - Use secrets manager (Vercel env vars, AWS Secrets Manager, etc.)
#  - Enable audit logging in Firebase
#
# VERCEL DEPLOYMENT:
#  - Use Project Settings > Environment Variables
#  - Add variables for Production, Preview, Development environments separately
#  - Use Vercel's built-in secrets management
#  - Enable automatic deployments from main branch
#
# DOCKER/KUBERNETES DEPLOYMENT:
#  - Build Docker image with no embedded secrets
#  - Use Kubernetes Secrets or external secrets operator
#  - Mount secrets as environment variables or files
#  - Use secrets rotation strategy (Sealed Secrets, External Secrets Operator)
#
# ==============================================================================
# CRITICAL VARIABLES CHECKLIST FOR PRODUCTION
# ==============================================================================
#
# The following variables MUST be configured for production:
#
# TIER 1 - ABSOLUTELY REQUIRED (App will not start without these):
#  [ ] NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_API_KEY
#  [ ] NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN
#  [ ] NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID
#  [ ] NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET
#  [ ] FIREBASE_ADMIN_CLIENT_EMAIL
#  [ ] FIREBASE_ADMIN_PRIVATE_KEY
#  [ ] GEMINI_API_KEY (if using Gemini features)
#
# TIER 2 - IMPORTANT (App works but features disabled):
#  [ ] FAL_KEY (audio transcription)
#  [ ] CRON_SECRET (scheduled quota resets)
#  [ ] NODE_ENV (set to "production")
#  [ ] NEXT_PUBLIC_BASE_URL (correct domain)
#
# TIER 3 - RECOMMENDED (Enhanced observability):
#  [ ] NEXT_PUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN (error tracking)
#
# ==============================================================================
# COST MONITORING & QUOTAS
# ==============================================================================
#
# This application uses paid APIs. Monitor costs:
#
# Google Gemini API:
#  - Free tier: 60 requests per minute
#  - Paid: $0.075 per 1M input tokens, $0.30 per 1M output tokens
#  - Dashboard: https://console.cloud.google.com/
#  - Estimate: ~$0.001 per study material generation
#
# Google Imagen 4:
#  - Paid: $0.04 per image (approximately)
#  - Limit: Max 2 images per material generation
#  - Dashboard: Same as Gemini
#  - Estimate: ~$0.08 per material with images
#
# FAL.ai (Whisper):
#  - Paid: ~$0.0001 per second of audio
#  - Video transcription: ~$0.005 per minute
#  - Dashboard: https://fal.ai/dashboard
#  - Estimate: ~$0.05 per 10-minute lecture
#
# Firebase Firestore:
#  - Free tier: 50K reads, 20K writes, 20K deletes per day
#  - Paid: $0.06 per 100K reads, $0.18 per 100K writes
#  - Dashboard: https://console.firebase.google.com/
#  - Estimate: Minimal cost unless very heavy usage
#
# Cost Optimization Tips:
#  1. Implement request batching for Gemini API
#  2. Cache generated materials when possible
#  3. Set daily quotas per user (implemented)
#  4. Use cheaper models when possible (Gemini 1.5 Flash)
#  5. Monitor and alert on unusual usage patterns
#
# ==============================================================================
# SECURITY BEST PRACTICES
# ==============================================================================
#
# 1. SECRET ROTATION:
#    - Rotate FIREBASE_ADMIN_PRIVATE_KEY every 90 days
#    - Rotate CRON_SECRET every 30 days
#    - Rotate API keys if exposed or staff leaves
#
# 2. LEAST PRIVILEGE:
#    - Firebase: Use custom security rules, limit database access
#    - Google Cloud: Create separate service accounts for different purposes
#    - Firestore: Enable field-level security rules
#
# 3. MONITORING:
#    - Monitor Sentry for error spikes
#    - Set up cost alerts in Google Cloud and FAL.ai
#    - Review Firebase access logs regularly
#    - Monitor API error rates and quotas
#
# 4. VERSION CONTROL:
#    - NEVER commit .env.local, .env.production, or any .env.* files
#    - Use .gitignore to prevent accidental commits
#    - If secrets are exposed:
#      1. Immediately revoke the secret (delete API key)
#      2. Regenerate new credentials
#      3. Clean git history with git-filter-repo or BFG Repo-Cleaner
#      4. Notify users and affected services
#
# 5. INCIDENT RESPONSE:
#    - Have a process for handling compromised credentials
#    - Maintain audit logs of who accessed sensitive data
#    - Practice regular incident response drills
#
# ==============================================================================
# TROUBLESHOOTING GUIDE
# ==============================================================================
#
# Issue: "Missing required Firebase environment variables"
#  Solution: Verify all NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_* variables are set
#  Debug: Check Firebase Console > Project Settings > Web App Config
#
# Issue: "Firebase Admin initialization failed"
#  Solution: Check FIREBASE_ADMIN_PRIVATE_KEY and FIREBASE_ADMIN_CLIENT_EMAIL
#  Debug: Verify service account JSON in Firebase Console
#  Common: Newline escaping in environment variables (\n vs actual newlines)
#
# Issue: "Gemini API key invalid"
#  Solution: Check GEMINI_API_KEY at https://aistudio.google.com/app/apikey
#  Debug: Ensure APIs enabled in Google Cloud Console
#  Common: API key format should start with "AIzaSy"
#
# Issue: "FAL.ai authentication failed"
#  Solution: Verify FAL_KEY at https://fal.ai/dashboard/keys
#  Debug: Check API key hasn't expired or been rotated
#
# Issue: "Cron job returns 401 Unauthorized"
#  Solution: Verify CRON_SECRET matches scheduler configuration
#  Debug: Check Authorization header in Vercel/scheduler config
#  Note: Must be: "Bearer {CRON_SECRET_VALUE}"
#
# Issue: "Sentry events not being captured"
#  Solution: Check NEXT_PUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN format
#  Debug: Verify DSN hasn't changed in Sentry dashboard
#  Note: Must start with "https://"
#
